= Evolution of Echinodermata =

* Relations of extant clades well-understood
* Calcichordate hypothesis disproven
* No agreement (or even theories?) on origin of Eleutherozoa
* No agreement on whether Crinoids originate from Blastozoa or elsewhere
* No agreement on general Blastozoan phylogeny
* No agreement on placement of Cyclocystoidea
* No clear agreement on ancestry of Edrioasteroidea to other groups
* No agreement on placement of "carpoids" and Helicoplacoidea
* No agreement on ''Arkarua''
* No agreementon Vetulocystida
* No agreement on ''Yanjiahella''
* No agreement over stereom-first vs pentaradiality-first

== Theories ==

* Lovén's Law
* Ocular Plate Rule (OPR)
* Extraxial/Axial Theory (EAT)
* Paedomorphic Ambulacra Reduction (PAR)
* Universal Element Homology (UEH)
* Phylogenetics

== Ambulacrarian Context ==

* Cambroernids suggest stalked tentacle-feeding ancestor
** ''Herpetogaster'' has chordate-like segments and no post-anal tail
* ''Yanjihella'' likely ambulacrarian
** Plated theca, no evidence of stereom, but also no evidence of absence
** Stem-echinoderm position favors stereom-first, but not accepted by all
** Stem-hemichordate or stem-ambulacrarian compatible with pentaradiality-first
* Vetulocystida is mysterious
** Neither pentaradial nor armored
** One structure looks like echinoderm anal cone
** Stem-echinoderm position more likely with stereom-first
** Could be stem-ambulacrarian or even stem-Chordate or stem-Deuterostome

